.TH RDOWNLOADER 1 "2026-10-22" "rdownloader" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rdownloader \- download manager with Tor, multi-part downloads and a terminal UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdownloader
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rdownloader
downloads files through the Tor network using an embedded Arti client.
Each download is split into parts that use separate circuits, failed parts are retried,
and interrupted downloads can be resumed.
Without a URL the terminal UI starts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-parts " \fIN\fR"
Number of parts per download (1\-10). Servers without byte-range support are downloaded over one connection.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR"
Target file or directory.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
No terminal UI; log progress to the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
No terminal UI. Serve the JSON-RPC/REST control API on
.B rpc_listen
(default 127.0.0.1:8765) instead.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tor\-clients " \fIN\fR"
Deprecated and ignored. A single Tor client isolates every part.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tor
Do not start Tor. For testing only; downloads need Tor and do not run in this mode.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH TERMINAL UI KEYS
.TP
.B a
Add a URL.
.TP
.B i
Import links from a text or M3U file.
.TP
.B v
Import links from the clipboard.
.TP
.B Enter
Show or hide details (parts, speed, ETA, Tor state) of the selected download.
.TP
.BR p ", " r ", " c ", " d
Pause, resume, cancel, remove the selected download.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Switch tab.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH LINK GRABBER KEYS
In the LinkGrabber tab the links are collected first and downloaded only after the confirmation.
.TP
.BR a ", " i ", " v ", " c
Collect a URL, the links of a list file, the clipboard, or crawl a page for links.
.TP
.BR Space ", " p ", " A
Mark the selected link, the whole package, or all links.
.TP
.BR f ", " F
Exclude the host or the file type of the selected link.
.TP
.B x
Remove the selected link or package.
.TP
.B Enter
Transfer the marked links into the download queue.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.toml
In the platform config directory under
.IR rdownloader/ ,
for example
.I ~/.config/rdownloader/config.toml
on Linux and
.I ~/Library/Application Support/rdownloader/config.toml
on macOS. Created on first start. Keys:
.BR max_parts ", " max_retries ", " max_speed_kib " (KiB/s, 0 = unlimited), " bridges ", " download_dir ", " temp_dir ", " tor_data_dir ", " user_agent ", " connect_timeout_secs ", " read_timeout_secs ", " log_level ", " rpc_listen ", " rpc_token .
.TP
.TP
.I downloads.json
Download history and session state, in the platform data directory under
.IR rdownloader/ .
Stored unencrypted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter; overrides
.BR log_level .
.TP
.B RDOWNLOADER_LANG
Interface language code (BenR or BdeR). Overrides the BlanguageR
setting in the config file.
.SH HEADLESS API
With
.B \-\-daemon
the queue is available over HTTP:
.B GET /api/jobs
lists jobs,
.B POST /api/jobs
adds one from a JSON body such as
.BR {\"url\":\ \"https://example.com/file.bin\"} ,
.BR POST " /api/jobs/" id "/pause|resume|cancel"
controls a job, and
.BR DELETE " /api/jobs/" id
removes it. JSON-RPC 2.0 is served at
.BR POST " /rpc" .
.B GET /health
reports readiness. Without
.B rpc_token
the server only binds to loopback. Requests must use a local
.B Host
header (localhost, a loopback address, or the bind address); state-changing
requests with a body need
.B Content-Type: application/json
and are rejected when their
.B Origin
names another site.
.SH SECURITY
Anonymity depends on Tor. Plain http URLs are visible to the exit relay; prefer https.
Local state files are not encrypted. See
.I docs/threat-model.md
in the source tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tor (1)
